			<div class="content" id="post-content-4010778">
									

<p>I'm not sure what's going on here. If SCP-4947 doesn't represent the number of actual human deaths by dysentery, but only the number reported, how does filling the numbers with a false report eliminate actual human deaths entirely? There should be plenty which are never directly reported that still occur. Is stating that there are no actual human deaths a false statement designed to not add to the number of deaths reported by Sunny Skies Analytics?</p>
<p>This seems to underestimate how common dysentery is and how huge an undertaking it would be to conceal the disappearance of all dysentery deaths. Is this an intentional undercurrent to the SCP or an oversight?</p>
<p>I personally don't like future SCPs, but this one seems especially bad to me because it's not just supposing an alternate future (with future tech or whatever) but just has to be set at a different time otherwise the core concept of the SCP is easily disprovable.</p>
<p>I actually quite like the idea here and the aspects I find confusing could potentially be as intended (something that appears quite simple but has a lot of strange aspects after thinking about it for a while). However, as it stands it's just confusing to me, not strange-confusing.</p>

