<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The twist is that the total number of <em>reported</em> deaths is equal to Fibonacci(n), which is anomalous behavior. However, since it is off reports, then reporting Fibonacci(n) deaths means that there can not be any more actual deaths that could possibly be reported. Thus, by reporting the deaths, the anomaly is exploited and all deaths by dysentery are prevented around the world. So it's a net positive.</p>
<p>Of course, if they stop reporting false deaths, it's a disaster.</p>
